; M4 gate: :keyon retrigger on the FM3 independent-operator tracks — each
; operator re-attacks its OWN $28 bit while the others keep sounding
; (driver.md §13.4).
;
; op2 rolls under a held op1 and op4: every retrigger has to drop and restore
; bit $20 alone, leaving $10 and $80 set through the whole bar. The shared
; 4-bit mask is the trap — a retrigger written as a plain key-off/key-on of
; channel 3 would silence the other three with it. op3 rolls on a different
; :step so the two interleave, including a frame where both fire.
;
; `[0 :hold 1]` (not a leading 1) because a macro's step 0 lands in the note's
; own frame, where the driver re-attacks and the editor treats the sample as
; the note's own key-on — a divergence of its own, on every channel, that this
; gate is not the place to pin down.
(def kit :alg 4 :fb 3
  :ar1 31 :dr1 4 :sr1 0 :rr1 6 :sl1 1 :tl1 24 :ml1 2
  :ar2 31 :dr2 9 :sr2 3 :rr2 9 :sl2 3 :tl2 8  :ml2 1
  :ar3 31 :dr3 9 :sr3 3 :rr3 9 :sl3 3 :tl3 28 :ml3 4
  :ar4 31 :dr4 4 :sr4 0 :rr4 6 :sl4 1 :tl4 4  :ml4 1)
(fm3 :tempo 120 kit)
(fm3-1 :oct 5 :len 1  c)
(fm3-2 :oct 4 :len 1  (macro :keyon [0 :hold 1] :step 4f) c)
(fm3-3 :oct 3 :len 1  (macro :keyon [0 :hold 1] :step 6f) c)
(fm3-4 :oct 4 :len 1  g)
